# OpenVario layout

This checkout builds a Yocto image. It is not the flight-computer
application.

- Product recipes, machines, and image contents: `meta-openvario/`.
  That directory is its own git repository. A commit there does not
  update this repo until the gitlink commit changes.
- `bitbake/`, `openembedded-core/`, `meta-openembedded/`, `meta-arm/`,
  `meta-sunxi/`, `meta-raspberrypi/`, and `meta-rauc/` are upstream
  pins. Fix an OpenVario issue with a `.bbappend` in `meta-openvario`,
  not by editing those trees.
- Layer branch is `scarthgap` (`LAYERSERIES_COMPAT` includes it).
  This repository's branch is `main`.
- Generated build state stays untracked: `conf/`, `tmp/`, `downloads/`,
  `sstate-cache/`, `cache/`, `build/`. See `.gitignore`.
- Starting config is `meta-openvario/conf/templates/default/`.
  `local.conf.sample` selects `DISTRO ?= "ovlinux"` and
  `PACKAGE_CLASSES ?= "package_ipk"`.
- Machines are `meta-openvario/conf/machine/ov-*.conf`. `README.md`
  lists the boards pilots build. `SHORT_OV_MACHINE` becomes part of
  the image file name.
